# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the tp4/s7 window (the ship-7 candidate; scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over
# .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/s7 and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN, ONE TAG AT A TIME (wait for the run to finish; never cancel a running card job).
# Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a registry: the cards are resolved at run time. The jobs are templates only: no tag is pushed from the branch by its author. ORDER.txt and
# ORDER-SHIP.txt have the order, the stop rules, the minutes and the read rules of the two runs.
# ONE IMAGE FOR THE WHOLE WINDOW AND THE SHIP: C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-s7-1 is a PLACEHOLDER for the tag B0 builds from the pushed branch head WITH the K64j-OQ graft and the ship-7 profile baked as the serving default
# (sed -i 's/tp4-s7-1/<tag>/' *.env). A commit of a file the image carries needs a new B0 build and a new tag in every template. This window never stops, starts or hands back the node agent.
# C2_MODEL_REPO / C2_MODEL_REVISION (qwen_c2_checkpoint.py): a job that carries them serves the Swift checkpoint (what production serves) from its own converted-weight directory; the keys are the same in every
# smoke and prefix job of this pack, so each pair differs by the profile alone. The replay and build steps do not forward the selection (the job reader refuses the keys beside them): they run the base checkpoint.
# R1 (TIMED, the CONTROL of the RESTORE pair; the test that exists for the threaded upload, a returning session evicted to the host tier and restored): the tier-timed cycle
# at ~64k, ~128k and ~254k (c2_prefix_gate.py --plan tier-upload-timed-control: a cold prefill, the device-resident hit, floods the size of the KV pool, the returning hit
# that restores from the host tier, and its cold twin; no row digests, no extent audit, the tier's own audits off, the digest check sampled) on the profile ship 6 serves,
# without the threaded upload (the CONTROL of the pair) c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-levern-w2-er-fx-traffic-s6. There is no restore-heavy smoke test (the smoke tests'
# returning turns restore too, but untimed and mixed with prefill): this is the prefix gate's own plan, one job a side, no new harness. THE PAIR: R1 control, R2 candidate,
# every boot a fresh reset, the ARC runner sets at ZERO for the job. READ each: the plan verdict PASS (every cold twin IDENTICAL to its returning hit), the "host tier
# restore" line of each returning turn (blocks, GB, ms, slices); then python3 scripts/ci/upload_restore_compare.py <R1 results> <R2 results> <R1 results> <R2 results> (it
# wants an ABAB; the single pair is passed twice, so its repeat floor reads 1: say so in the verdict). ESTIMATE: the restore ms down by at least 25 percent at 128k and
# 254k, the returning hit's TTFT not above the control's by more than 5 percent; the lever cannot change the returning request's own final prefill step or engine build (4.2
# to 4.8 s at 254k). UPLOAD (QWEN_PREFIX_TIER_IO_THREADS=4, QWEN_PREFIX_TIER_VERIFY_THREADS=4): the line "[PINDIAG] prefix: host tier upload on io_threads=4
# io_chunk_blocks=.. verify_threads=4 io_wrapped=1" once, a returning session restored through the threaded IO (the restore line and tier_io_write_blocks above 0 in the
# counters), NO "host tier upload latched off" line and NO "host tier upload fell back" line (a latch is a FAIL: the call was repeated through the serial code, so the
# answers are right and the lever is not working), zero digest failures. ESTIMATE: a 254k restore of about 1 s falls toward 0.4 to 0.6 s, so a returning turn's first token
# (5.4 to 6.5 s) gains under 0.5 s. RUN WITH THE CI PAUSED: the ARC runner sets are at ZERO for this job (ORDER, ARC-ZERO); no build, no CI push, no other job beside it.
# CHECKPOINT READ (the workflow passes c2_smoke_check.py --expect-checkpoint): the container log holds "[QWEN-C2] checkpoint
# ukisai/Swift-1.5-Qwen3.8-27b@b4c84d42903a8646b25857eb2827288d92ed85a4 key=... weight_cache=.../weights-ckpt/<key> base_cache=... (the base cache is not read or written)"
# once, a "weight cache ...: found" line (the cache the Swift window built; this pack never builds it) and the worker's "[QWEN-C2] checkpoint bound ..." line; the models
# answer names ukisai/Swift-1.5-Qwen3.8-27b. Duration (estimate): 45 minutes.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset prefix
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-s7-1
C2_MODEL_REPO=ukisai/Swift-1.5-Qwen3.8-27b
C2_MODEL_REVISION=b4c84d42903a8646b25857eb2827288d92ed85a4
C2_PREFIX_PLAN=tier-upload-timed-control
C2_PREFIX_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-levern-w2-er-fx-traffic-s6
C2_PREFIX_BASELINE=none
C2_BOX_MINUTES=90
